{"Added a new ROLLING_UPDATES enum entry when ROLLING_UPDATES_V1 and ROLLING_UPDATES_V2 already exist, creating a third feature identity that diverges from the established rolling-update feature family instead of the requested compatibility feature flag": 0.03880925849080086, "Operator update job invokes update-compatibility metadata and check commands without passing --features=rolling-updates flag, causing the job to fail with exit code 4 since the CLI now requires the feature to be enabled": 0.23661097884178162, "Exit code contract changed inconsistently - recreate is now exit code 3 and feature-disabled is exit code 4, whereas previously recreate used exit code 4, which will cause misclassification of results by operator logic and existing callers": 0.5756059288978577, "Documentation example for metadata command omits the required --features=rolling-updates flag, showing a command that will now fail with feature-disabled exit code instead of succeeding": 0.014723743312060833, "Custom image Dockerfile unconditionally enables --features=rolling-updates preview feature, hard-wiring it into all custom images regardless of whether the operator or CLI needs it, which is beyond the issue scope": 0.33808356523513794, "Feature gate check happens before validateConfig() is called, deviating from peer CLI commands pattern where inputs are validated first, causing users with missing --file argument to get feature-disabled error instead of missing-argument validation error": 0.212344229221344}